eligible if it is not constant and has at least \code{n_rows + 2} observed values.
Every rank is fitted on the same matrix, with the same values hidden, and is
scored on those values only. The holdout needs more than two values. The
\code{abb} columns take no part in tuning, and no value in them is held out.

\strong{The rank.} \code{crps} is the continuous ranked probability score of each
held-out value against its draws, on the scale of \code{obj}, averaged over the
held-out values. A lower score is better. \code{\link[=mipca_fit]{mipca_fit()}} fits the rank with
the lowest \code{crps} unless it is given another.

\strong{The noise.} \code{implied_nu} is the Student-t degrees of freedom that the
spread of the held-out values implies, \code{Inf} when they look Gaussian.
\code{implied_lo} and \code{implied_hi} are its bootstrap interval. \code{implied_nu} is the
raw reading. \code{\link[=mipca_fit]{mipca_fit()}} fits with \code{nu} set to \code{implied_nu}, or to \code{5} if
the reading is lower.

\strong{Failures.} A rank whose fit fails does not stop the call. Its row holds
the message in \code{error}, and its scores are \code{NA}.

\strong{Reproducibility.} With the same \code{seed}, the held-out values and the table
are the same. A given \code{seed} leaves R's random number stream as it was. With
\code{seed = NULL}, the same \code{\link[=set.seed]{set.seed()}} before the call gives the same table.
